From 1003c650f87545434fb49ada90d18009e08976df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:40:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] bittree model: track the safe locations

The segment model registers errno, stdout, stderr and stdin as safe
locations at start-up (collect_safe_locations). The bittree model has the
comment "Tracking safe locations" in eacsl_memory_init but never called
it: every check on a standard stream or on errno that reaches the runtime
(\valid of a copy of stdout, \object_pointer(stdout), the -rte
-warn-invalid-pointer guard of fputs(..., stdout), \valid(&errno) through
a pointer) failed in that model only.

Call collect_safe_locations in eacsl_memory_init. The bittree model does
not support threads (eacsl_pthread_create aborts), so one call covers the
program.

New test special/e-acsl-bittree-std-streams.c, run with both memory models
(dev configuration).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
